# Q29 (author, 2026-09-25: «одна ячейка там где объявление»; FABLE-OPUS-CODE-DATA-SPLIT-20260925-189
# c3c) numbered the two bare assignments of the argument `arg` as one cell, \[0]arg.  bafca4c (the author,
# 2026-09-28: assignment is not a declaration; an argument is its parameter) removes that cell: `arg: 1` and
# `arg: 2` change the activation's value and declare nothing, and `\[N]` numbers declarations -- there is
# none of arg, so \[0]arg is refused where it stands ("no such occurrence").
fn: mytest (int: arg) int
    arg: 1
    arg: 2
    if: \[0]arg != 2
        return: 1
    return: 0
end: mytest
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: mytest(0); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
